# Region Configuration Guide

## Configuration Structure

### Base Configuration
The base configuration for regions is defined in [internal/config/types.go](mdc:internal/config/types.go):
- `ChoreoEnvConfig`: Base configuration type for all environments
- Environment-specific settings (URLs, client IDs, etc.)

### Region-Specific Configurations

1. US Region (Default)
- Configuration in [internal/region/us_config.go](mdc:internal/region/us_config.go)
- Default production endpoints
- Development and staging environments for internal use

2. EU Region
- Configuration in [internal/region/eu_config.go](mdc:internal/region/eu_config.go)
- EU-specific endpoints and services
- Separate authentication endpoints

## Environment Management

### Environment Types
Each region supports three environments:
1. Production (prod) - Default for end users
2. Development (dev) - For internal development
3. Staging (stage) - For testing and validation

### Environment Selection
- End users: Always use production environment
- Developers: Can override using CHOREO_ENV environment variable
- Environment selection is region-aware

## Implementation Details

### Thread Safety
- Region selection uses mutex locks
- Concurrent access protection for configuration
- Safe region switching during operations

### Configuration Initialization
- US region initialized by default
- EU region configurations loaded on demand
- Environment configs initialized at startup

### Best Practices
1. Always use region-aware configuration getters
2. Check token validity when switching regions
3. Use environment variables only for development
4. Handle region-specific endpoints appropriately
